A: ArrayList.Test.cs

using System;
using System.Text;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Settings;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Exceptions;

using NUnit.Framework;
using ArrayList;
using PexAPIWrapper;

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    [TestFixture, PexClass]
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        [PexMethod]
        [PexExpectedException(typeof(System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException))]
        public void PUT_RemoveAtContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int index)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index >= 0 && index < arrList.Count);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_index = index;

            arrList.RemoveAt(index);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            bool New_arrListContainsOldIndex = arrList.Contains(Old_index);

            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_count", Old_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_count", New_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$Old_index", Old_index);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_index", Old_index);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_contains_OldIndex", New_arrListContainsOldIndex);
        }
    }
}

'In the test class, there is only one test method 'PUT_RemoveAtContract' testing the contract of RemoveAt method.
'In the precondition, I add the condition making sure the index is within the range of the list.'
'And, add the expect exception 'System.ArgumentOutOfRangeException' when the index out of the range.

Remember to change "ArrayList" and "PexAPIWrapper" to the corresponding namespaces of your project.

The class should be placed in the same namespace as your ArrayList class so that the NUnit framework can appropriately identify the test.

The PexMethod attribute tells Pex to instrument the method so that Pex can test it. The PexExpectedException attribute is used to specify that an exception of the specified type is expected from running this method. 

'An important thing to note is to create the correct conditions and correct assumptions for each method, as it helps Pex to work more effectively and generate more meaningful tests.'

Please note the condition and assumptions are very important and needs to be set according with the contract specification of the methods you are testing. If the assumption is false, then the test case can never be executed.

'Therefore, carefully considering and setting the condition and assumptions is the key to creating meaningful tests with Pex.'

Also always ensure that your Pex tests are covering all critical code paths of the methods you are testing and only testing the public interface of your classes and methods.

'Pex does its best to cover all valid input ranges, but still it can miss some rare cases.'

So in this code, we are testing the 'PUT_RemoveAtContract' which checks the contract of 'RemoveAt' method, setting the conditions and assumptions according to the method contract and specifying the expected exception.
Please replace "ArrayList" and "PexAPIWrapper" namespace as per your project's namespace.

Also, a Pex test is not a substitute for unit tests as it does not cover all cases and scenarios that could occur in all edge and corner cases. It is advisable to use them together. So, make sure to verify the test results with other tests to increase the thoroughness of your test suite.
!


